"""Prepared reference solution for ``weight_int8pack_mm``.

Per-channel int8 weight-only quantised GEMM: ``A`` is an fp16/bf16 activation
of shape ``(M, K)``, ``B`` is the int8 weight of shape ``(N, K)`` (one byte per
element, not bit-packed) and ``scales`` is a per-output-channel vector of shape
``(N,)``.  The result is ``(M, N)`` in ``A.dtype`` on ``A.device``.

The computation below is exactly the frozen master oracle
(``tests/test_weight_int8pack_mm.py::_ref_weight_int8pack_mm``) wrapped as the
injected candidate entrypoint ``run(A, B, scales)``:

    B_fp = B.to(A.dtype)
    result = torch.matmul(A, B_fp.T)
    result = result * scales.unsqueeze(0)

Contract preserved from the frozen Definition (outputs ``["out"]``,
``effects.mutates = []``, ``effects.returns_alias_of = {}``):
  * returns a freshly allocated tensor (no input is written, no aliasing);
  * output dtype equals the activation dtype, output device equals input device;
  * no tolerance, cast, seed or skip is introduced here.

The module deliberately does not import ``flag_gems`` and does not call the
Gems/ATen ``_weight_int8pack_mm`` export, so injecting it as the candidate
cannot re-enter the operator under test.
"""

import torch


def run(A, B, scales):
    B_fp = B.to(A.dtype)
    result = torch.matmul(A, B_fp.T)
    result = result * scales.unsqueeze(0)
    return result
